cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pulse-ep in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "pulse-ep: An open-source platform for programmatic access to CARTO electroanatomical mapping data"
abstract: >-
  pulse-ep is a Python package and web platform that parses CARTO 3
  (Biosense Webster) electroanatomical-mapping exports into a relational
  PostgreSQL database and exposes the data via a JWT-authenticated REST API,
  a browser-based 3D viewer (Three.js / WebGL), and a Python toolkit for
  custom analyses. It enables quantitative research on triangulated atrial
  surface meshes — including geodesic distance computation, surface-area
  integration over scalar intervals, and reference-catheter geometry analysis —
  that are not available in the clinical mapping system.
